<file path="public/assets/README-trainer-details.txt">
Trainer Details page: images to put in this folder
(the sandbox it was built in could not download from figma.com)

  trainer-bg.png     Figma node 48:67 "image 5"  -> export the ORIGINAL image.
                     Dark gym photo behind the page (the page darkens it by 70%).
  trainer-photo.png  Figma node 73:51 "image 7"  -> export the ORIGINAL image.
                     Sample trainer portrait. In production pass the real
                     photo with <TrainerDetails photoSrc="..." />.

fittrack-emblem.svg (the logo mark in the sidebar) is the same file the
Sign Up page already uses. If an image is missing the page still works:
grey box for the photo, plain dark background, no logo mark.
</file>

<file path="public/assets/README.txt">
Put these files from Figma in this folder (the sandbox this was built in
could not download from figma.com):

  gym-bg.png            Figma node 13:43 "image 3" -> export the ORIGINAL image.
                        Used by the Sign Up and Registration Details pages.
  fittrack-emblem.svg   Figma node 154:232 "fittrack-emblem" -> Export as SVG.
  payment-qr.png        Figma node 13:166 "image 4" -> export the image.
                        Sample QR for the Registration Details page. In production, pass
                        the real QR from your backend with <RegistrationDetails qrSrc=... />.
                        If this file is missing, a "QR code will appear here"
                        placeholder is shown instead.

All are referenced as /assets/<name> and served from /public, so no import is needed.
</file>

